{
  "schemaVersion": "1.0",
  "scriptId": "log-03-change-base-reciprocal-chains",
  "sourceType": "MANUAL",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Change of Base, Reciprocals, and Log Chains",
    "description": "Move between bases, use reciprocal logarithms, and collapse telescoping products or sums of logarithms.",
    "teachingApproach": "Start by measuring the same logarithm in a different base, then show the reciprocal relation as a one-line consequence. Use cancellation chains and reciprocal sums so learners see when a complicated expression is really one logarithm in disguise.",
    "targetDurationMinutes": 30,
    "sourceScope": "R.S. Aggarwal, Quantitative Aptitude for Competitive Examinations, Chapter 10, Logarithms. Teach log_a x = log_b x / log_b a and the reciprocal relation log_a b = 1/log_b a. Use these to evaluate mixed-base expressions such as log_9 27 and log_27 9, products like log_a b·log_b c, longer telescoping chains, and sums containing reciprocals such as 1/log_a x = log_x a. Include bases that are powers, using log_(a^q) x = (1/q)log_a x, and simple equal-power relations such as a^x=b^y. Learners should choose a common base that makes cancellation visible rather than converting everything blindly."
  },
  "startNodeId": "start",
  "nodes": {
    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's learn how to move a logarithm from one base to another.\n\nThis is useful when the original base looks awkward but another base makes the powers easy.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1": {
      "id": "teach_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "The change-of-base rule says:\n\nlog_a x = (log_b x)/(log_b a)\n\nThe new base b can be any convenient valid base.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1_step": {
      "id": "teach_1_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "For example, using common logs:\n\nlog₂8 = log8/log2.\nIf log8=0.9030 and log2=0.3010, the ratio is 3.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "q_1": {
      "id": "q_1",
      "type": "CHOICE",
      "content": {
        "text": "If log 8 = 0.9030 and log 2 = 0.3010, what is log₂8?",
